Dear PC NetHackers,

	The PC team is in the process of building the "offical" package
combining the executable, and support files for the MSDOS
environment.  It will be released as a *set* of files to allow disk transfer
of the game to PCs with only 360k floppy drives and a hard disk.  (The
actual exe is around 840k when put together).  This should be finished
shortly and will be available for anonymous ftp on linc.cis.upenn.edu.

	A further note will be forthcoming when this process has been
completed.

	There has been a been a lot of function & overlay manager optimization
done, and the difference in speed is quite noticeable (tease tease).
 
!*PLEASE NOTE*!

	If you decide to compile and distribute the overlay version of
MSDOS Nethack *do not* repeat *do NOT* include the termcap libraries in
the executable.  If you do so it is at your own risk.  These routines
are currently thought to be the cause of crashes in the MSDOS version,
and are under scrutiny by our team.
 
	To build without the termlib.lib make sure you proceed as follows:

1.	Enable the "#define TERMINFO" in config.h
	(Technically this should not make a difference but.....)

2.	Comment out the "#define TERMLIB" in pcconf.h.

3.	Comment out the line in the makefile that defines termlib.lib.

	This will ensure some degree of uniformity among patch level 7 releases
and provides for the most stable game.

	Should the termlib pass future testing, a messsage will be posted
saying that the are safe to include once more.

	Good luck patching.  30 Parts?!?.  Sheesh.

					For the PC team,

					Norm

P.S.	Please Oh Please no requests for the binary yet.  I aint got the
	official version yet either!
